### 1. Sawyerville–Eoline Tornado – April 27, 2011（官方风暴调查）

- **标题**: Sawyerville-Eoline Tornado - April 27, 2011  
- **URL**: https://www.weather.gov/bmx/event_04272011sawyerville  
- **发布方/作者**: National Weather Service Birmingham, Alabama (Weather Forecast Office)  
- **发布日期/更新日期**: 页面未列明具体日期（内容与事件对应为2011年4月27日之后的调查报告）；标记为 null  
- **来源类型**: 官方政府/天气局事件页面（NWS 风暴调查）  
- **触发查询语句**: `National Weather Service Birmingham Alabama "Sawyerville" "Eoline" tornado April 27 2011 storm survey`  
- **与检索目标的相关性**:  
  - 直接是 NWS Birmingham 对 2011 年 Sawyerville–Eoline 龙卷风的官方风暴调查页面。  
  - 提供 EF 级别、最大风速、路径长度、宽度、起止时间和坐标，以及沿路径各地的详细损害描述。  
  - 属于 2011 年 4 月 27 日“超级爆发”（Historic Outbreak）的一部分并提及警报信息，可用于气象背景的局部描述。

- **读取到的正文（节选，保留原始格式与关键数据）**:

  页面顶部为 NWS Birmingham 页眉，其核心调查内容包括：

  > ***Sawyerville-Eoline (Greene, Hale and Bibb Counties) EF-3 Tornado April 27, 2011***

  关键参数表格（原文要点）：

  - **Rating:** EF-3  
  - **Estimated Maximum Wind:** 145 mph  
  - **Injuries/Fatalities:** 50 Injuries / 7 Fatalities  
  - **Damage Path Length:** 72.13 miles  
  - **Maximum Path Width:** 1760 yards (1 mile)  
  - **Approximate Start Point/Time:** 32.6152 / -88.0543 at 530 pm  
  - **Approximate End Point/Time:** 33.1524 / -86.9898 at 655 pm  

  详细损害与路径叙述（忠实摘录并略做分段，以便引用；加粗为原文中的强调）：

  > **National Weather Service meteorologists surveyed multiple tracks across Greene, Hale and Bibb Counties. It has been determined that the damage was consistent with a strong 
tornado. The tornado touched down in far southwest Greene County near the Tombigbee River just West of Tishabee on County Road 69 near Head Drive, and headed northeast across rural 
Greene County north of Forkland. At least 4 mobile homes, 3 outbuildings, and 2 churches were damaged or destroyed along with numerous trees. Two minor injuries were noted in Greene 
County. The track started as an EF-1 but increased to an EF-2 rating while in Greene County.**

  > **The tornado crossed the Black Warrior River and into Hale County west of Sawyerville. The tornado crossed AL Route 14, just north of Sawyerville, where it intensifyed to an EF-3
rating with winds of 145 mph. As the tornado continued northeast, it crossed CR 18, CR 21, AL Hwy 69 south of Harper Hill, and CR 29 east of Ingram. Extensive structural damage was 
noted in the these locations, which resulted in at least 40 injuries and 6 fatalities. Numerous mobile homes and single family homes and one church were damaged or destroyed. 
Thousands of trees were knocked down. The tornado moved into the Talladega National Forest near Ingram, where it caused significant tree damage to the Bibb County line.**

  > **The tornado tracked northeastward where it caused significant tree damage in the national forest. The tornado moved through Eoline and caused significant structural damage 
consistent with an EF-3 rating and winds of 145 mph. Numerous mobile homes and single family homes sustained minor to major damage. A dozen mobile homes and single family homes were 
destroyed. In addition, the Eoline Fire Dept and another business were destroyed. One fatality occurred in a vehicle near the fire dept. At least 10 other injuries were noted. The 
tornado continued northeast and crossed AL Hwy 5, south of West Blocton where it weakened slightly to an EF-2 with winds of 125 mph. Several mobile homes and single family homes 
sustained major damage or were destroyed near CR 26. Along the path, thousands of trees were downed. The tornado continued to weaken and lifted just northeast of Marvel.**

  > **Tornado Warnings were in effect for Greene, Hale and Bibb Counties from 450 pm until 745 pm.**

  页面还包含雷达图像链接等“Radar Data”部分（图像链接列举略）：

  - Radar Image: `/images/bmx/significant_events/2011/042711/sawyerville/r2255.gif` 等

  该页面整体为一次长路径强龙卷风的官方文档，涵盖路径沿线地名（Tishabee、Sawyerville、Ingram、Eoline、West Blocton、Marvel 等）、起止坐标与时间、伤亡数字，以及 EF 等级随路径变化（EF-1 
→ EF-2 → EF-3 → EF-2 → dissipated）的描述，可作为撰写 Wikipedia 风格条目的主要技术来源。

