      "statement": "The Sawyerville–Eoline tornado of April 27, 2011 was rated EF-3 with estimated maximum winds of about 145 mph, a path length of approximately 72.13 miles, and a 
maximum width of about 1760 yards, resulting in 50 injuries and 7 fatalities as it tracked across Greene, Hale, and Bibb Counties in Alabama.",
